From 3e4639882be5b46c2ea4ea2c5a73855e78857831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roland Mueller <roland.m.mueller@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:16:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make terms under roots and in fractions respond to hover
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Marked terms ignore hover and click when they sit under a square root,
in the denominator of a fraction, or in a lower row of an aligned block.
The equation looks fine, so the bug is easy to miss: in the bundled
examples it affects 7 terms in Maxwell's equations, P(E) in Bayes'
theorem, Z and T in the grand canonical ensemble, and ħ in the path
integral.

The cause is two invisible layout elements that KaTeX places on top of
the visible math, so they receive the mouse events instead:

- \sqrt draws the radical sign as a 400em-wide SVG (.hide-tail) that is
  clipped to size but still covers the whole expression under the root.
- Every vertical list (.vlist-t2: fractions, sums with limits, aligned
  rows) ends with an empty row that only reserves space below the
  baseline. It is position: relative and comes last in the DOM, so it is
  painted over the lower part of the list.

Neither element contains anything clickable, so pointer-events: none
on them changes nothing visually and lets events reach the terms below.
The rule goes in both places that render equations: the live view
(EquationDisplay.vue) and the standalone HTML export (htmlExport.ts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/components/equation/EquationDisplay.vue | 8 ++++++++
 src/export/htmlExport.ts                    | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/components/equation/EquationDisplay.vue b/src/components/equation/EquationDisplay.vue
index e0b5a16..c70ee15 100644
--- a/src/components/equation/EquationDisplay.vue
+++ b/src/components/equation/EquationDisplay.vue
@@ -189,6 +189,14 @@ onUnmounted(() => resizeObserver?.disconnect());
   margin: 0;
 }
 
+/* KaTeX overlays that would swallow hovers on marked terms:
+   the radical is a 400em-wide SVG drawn over the radicand, and the empty
+   depth row of a vertical list (fractions, sums, aligned) covers the lower half */
+#equation-container :deep(.hide-tail),
+#equation-container :deep(.vlist-t2 > .vlist-r:last-child) {
+  pointer-events: none;
+}
+
 .selection-overlay {
   position: absolute;
   top: 0;
diff --git a/src/export/htmlExport.ts b/src/export/htmlExport.ts
index 2e54871..42bb639 100644
--- a/src/export/htmlExport.ts
+++ b/src/export/htmlExport.ts
@@ -185,6 +185,14 @@ export function exportToHTML(
       font-weight: 600;
     }
 
+    /* KaTeX overlays that would swallow hovers on marked terms:
+       the radical is a 400em-wide SVG drawn over the radicand, and the empty
+       depth row of a vertical list (fractions, sums, aligned) covers the lower half */
+    .katex .hide-tail,
+    .katex .vlist-t2 > .vlist-r:last-child {
+      pointer-events: none;
+    }
+
     /* Interactive term effects */
     [class*="term-"] {
       transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
-- 
